Harbour Drone
=============

Laptop shows a 3D harbour; a phone flies the drone over the internet; real Trincomalee wind pushes it.

  /             laptop world (Three.js)
  /controller/  phone controller (two touch sticks + reset)

Setup
-----
1. npm install
2. Create a Supabase project, copy .env.example to .env and fill in the URL and anon key.
3. npm run dev        (laptop: http://localhost:5173/)

Deploy
------
npx vercel --prod, with VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY set as environment
variables in the Vercel project. Open the site on the laptop and scan the QR code with the phone.

Controls
--------
Phone:    left stick = altitude, right stick = move, RESET
Keyboard: W/S = altitude, arrows = move, R = reset (works without Supabase)

Goal: take off from the green pad, fly through the three rings (+100 each) and land gently
back on the pad (+100, plus a point per second left) before the 60-second clock runs out.
Touching the sea costs 50 and sends you back to the pad. Let go of the sticks and the real
Trincomalee wind carries the drone the way the arrow points.
